Appendix F: The Equivalent Effective Stratospheric Chlorine (EESC) Metric

F.1 Definition

EESC is a single metric that quantifies the total ozone-depleting potential of all halogen species in the stratosphere, weighted by their ozone depletion potential (ODP) and adjusted for their release efficiency.

 EESC(t) = \sum_i \alpha_i \cdot ODP_i \cdot n_i \cdot \Gamma_i(t) 

where:

·  i  indexes each chlorine- and bromine-containing species,
·  \alpha_i  is the number of Cl or Br atoms per molecule,
·  ODP_i  is the ozone depletion potential relative to CFC-11,
·  n_i  is the number of molecules released at the surface at time  t ,
·  \Gamma_i(t)  is the age-of-air spectrum dependent release efficiency (fraction reaching the stratosphere).

