Appendix L: The Brewer-Dobson Circulation and Transport Timescales

L.1 Circulation Structure

The Brewer-Dobson Circulation (BDC) is the large-scale stratospheric circulation driven by breaking planetary and gravity waves. It consists of:

· Upwelling in the tropics,
· Poleward transport in the middle and upper stratosphere,
· Downwelling at mid- and high-latitudes.

L.2 Transport Timescales

Pathway Typical Timescale
Troposphere to tropical lower stratosphere 1–3 months
Tropical lower stratosphere to mid-latitudes 3–5 years
Tropical lower stratosphere to poles 5–7 years
Full stratospheric transit 4–6 years
ODS lifetime in stratosphere 5–10 years (Cl), 2–4 years (Br)

These timescales explain why emission reductions at the surface take years to decades to affect stratospheric halogen loading.

